  "groundingSupports": [
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 798,
        "endIndex": 1024,
        "text": "#### Candidates [0] & [13]: Mistral AI Raises €3B Series D at €21B Valuation\n* **Confirmed:** Mistral AI officially announced a €3 billion Series D funding round at a post-money valuation exceeding €21 billion ($24.4B)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1026,
        "endIndex": 1128,
        "text": "Samsung Electronics led the round, with Scaleup Europe Fund (managed by EQT) and PSG Equity co-leading"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1130,
        "endIndex": 1259,
        "text": "New backers include BlackRock, Advent, and the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg; existing backers including Nvidia and ASML participated"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        2,
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1261,
        "endIndex": 1384,
        "text": "Capital will be used to expand frontier model research, compute capacity, and sovereign European data center infrastructure"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        0,
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1386,
        "endIndex": 1499,
        "text": "* **Caveats:** Mistral’s valuation nearly doubled from €11.7 billion in September 2025 (Series C led by ASML)"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        3
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1501,
        "endIndex": 1625,
        "text": "Reported targets to build up to 1 GW of European data center capacity by 2030 represent long-term infrastructure commitments"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1706,
        "endIndex": 1963,
        "text": "#### Candidate [5]: China Targets 9,800 Eflops AI Compute Capacity by 2030\n* **Confirmed:** China’s Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT) released a 2026–2030 five-year plan targeting 9,800 eflops of intelligent compute capacity by 2030"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "segment": {
        "startIndex": 1965,
        "endIndex": 2111,
        "text": "The plan calls for 3.8 trillion yuan (~$532B) in cumulative IT infrastructure investment and sets targets for 100,000-card AI accelerator clusters"
      },
      "groundingChunkIndices": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
